# Code owners are requested for review automatically. Review is not currently
# enforced by a ruleset: with two maintainers and no outside contributors,
# enforcement would only block their own direct pushes to main.
#
# The list is deliberately short. It covers what is normative, what is
# distributed, and what governs the project — not everything that is published.
# docs/, examples/ and README.md are left out on purpose: welcoming edits and
# then demanding two-party review on a typo is friction without a return.
#
# Note the property this buys for free: GitHub does not let an author approve
# their own pull request, so a change to SPEC.md written by one maintainer is
# reviewed by the other. That is the same separation the specification itself
# requires of policy files (SPEC 8), applied to the document that states it.

# Normative and executable artifacts
/SPEC.md                    @Argyronix/maintainers
/schema/                    @Argyronix/maintainers
/hooks/                     @Argyronix/maintainers
/skills/lorm/               @Argyronix/maintainers

# Distribution, CI and governance
/.claude-plugin/            @Argyronix/maintainers
/.github/workflows/         @Argyronix/maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @Argyronix/maintainers
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @Argyronix/maintainers
/SECURITY.md                @Argyronix/maintainers
/LICENSE                    @Argyronix/maintainers
/NOTICE                     @Argyronix/maintainers
